  nonce: 5dfc  # 5dfc
  message: "DONE in PR #1037 (CI green; merged from this state).\n\nTHE CLAIM AND THE CORRECTION. docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1317 said an\nout-of-taxonomy analyzer that finds no files is recorded in\n`limits.skipped_passes` \"either way\". It is not.\n\nEVIDENCE -- re-measured on canonical dev (e71fe45cbe), NOT reused from the\nfiling. This re-run was necessary rather than ceremonial: the INV-homur\npre-filter fix landed in between and changes `profile.languages` for five\nlanguages, which could have moved the routing itself. It did not.\n\n    out-of-taxonomy analyzers: 35\n      -> analysis_runs : 27   (26 of them with files_analyzed == 0)\n      -> skipped_passes:  8\n      -> neither       :  0\n\nSo 26 land in analysis_runs carrying silence_reason=no_candidate_files, and\nonly 8 land where the spec said. Identical to the numbers filed on 2026-09-17,\nso the finding is stable across the pre-filter change.\n\nTHE 8, BROKEN DOWN, because the filing said 7 and the measurement says 8 and\nthat discrepancy had to be resolved rather than rounded:\n\n    matlab meson puppet racket robot scheme scss   -> bare AnalysisResult()  (7)\n    rust_analyzer                                  -> backend_disabled       (1)\n\nThe 7 are exactly the seven named in collect_analyzer_result's own branch\ncomment. The 8th reaches skipped_passes by the separate opt-in-backend route\nthe spec already documents elsewhere, so it is not part of the \"found no\nfiles\" population this row is about. The filing's 7 was right.\n\nWHAT THE SENTENCE SAYS NOW. \"Either way\" is replaced by the three actual\nroutes, with the discriminator named at each: taxonomy membership decides\npre-filter vs dispatch, and the DISPATCHED ones then split by their own return\nstyle (bare AnalysisResult -> skipped_passes; a run with files_analyzed == 0\n-> analysis_runs). It also now states plainly that a consumer asking \"which\npasses had no input?\" must read BOTH hosts and should use\npass_silence.census_silence(), which unions over the pass CATALOGUE rather\nthan over the two lists -- because a pass in neither would otherwise be\ninvisible (WI-didag).\n\nSCOPE NOTE. This row is documentation-only and the behaviour it describes is\nunchanged; the Closure-Evidence Discipline's behavioural-repro requirement is\nnot triggered, but the measurement above is cited anyway because the sentence's\ncorrectness IS a measurable claim.\n\nNOT STRADDLED. The rename of skip_reason_code -> silence_reason (WI-mamiv\nverdict A) landed in the same PR only because it edits the same paragraph;\nfixing them separately would have meant writing section 1317 twice. The\nrouting itself is deliberately unchanged -- that remains the owner's call\nunder ADR-0056 item 5."  # 5dfc
